		<category><![CDATA[Top of Homepage]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://bridgemi.com/?p=83479</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Progressive victories in the midterm elections have reignited calls for 'Medicare for All' as voters struggle with rising healthcare costs, but critics warn of ‘huge' political risks.]]></description>
		
		
		
							<thumbnail_position>default</thumbnail_position>
					<media:content type="image/jpeg" url="https://i0.wp.com/bridgemi.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/Bogan-scaled-e1793982862826.jpg?fit=1024%2C683&#038;ssl=1">
												<media:description><![CDATA[Kim Bogan, an emergency room nurse in Michigan, has spent the past year campaigning for Abdul El-Sayed, because she believes &#039;Medicare for All&#039; is the best way to fix a broken healthcare system. The patients she sees coming into the ER have often put off getting care, even as their conditions deteriorated. (Kate Wells/KFF Health News)]]></media:description>
